          "sender_principal_id": "human",
          "worker_id": null,
          "execution_id": null,
          "body": "PRIVATE_GROUP_EXCLUSION_SENTINEL_P08. This is a private direct conversation, not a group export. Investigate one public documentation question about keyboard focus indicators using your own public query and research tools. Retrieve a relevant public page, give a concise sourced answer with limitations, and retain its source in this private work scope. Do not share private queries/history into other conversations or future working groups.",
          "request_id": null,
          "response_to": null,
          "created_at": "2026-10-05T19:52:30.703Z"
        },
        {
          "cursor": 26,
          "message_id": "cmessage_e01ef0de-f137-425f-bd42-39f2dc45b2a0",
          "conversation_id": "conversation_11aa81e3-f884-4bc2-9b0d-9c156d5a198e",
          "sender_principal_id": "principal_d9835669-11bc-48d3-ba13-42e15654f41e",
          "worker_id": "worker_14cbf2db-6d94-433c-a546-35c5d66b8f93",
          "execution_id": "execution_327aabd8-87f1-4610-b2e2-9c96bf918e3f",
          "body": "**Public documentation finding:** W3C’s WCAG 2.2 guidance for [2.4.7 Focus Visible](https://www.w3.org/WAI/WCAG22/Understanding/focus-visible) says keyboard-operable interfaces need a mode in which the focus indicator is visible. It should remain visible while keyboard focus is shown, rather than timing out. This is a Level AA criterion; W3C lists CSS `:focus-visible` as one possible technique, provided it produces a visible indicator.\n\n**Limitations:** The linked “Understanding” page is explanatory, not itself the normative WCAG requirement. It does not prescribe one indicator design; the separate 2.4.13 Focus Appearance criterion gives additional Level AAA guidance. I reviewed the retrieved page text, not a particular website’s implementation. The source is retained only in this private conversation’s research scope.",
          "request_id": "reply_a101af47-d28f-4adb-97b9-e93861c863a8",
          "response_to": "reply_a101af47-d28f-4adb-97b9-e93861c863a8",
          "created_at": "2026-10-05T19:52:54.224Z"
        },
        {
          "cursor": 43,
          "message_id": "cmessage_42a12cee-c6ba-4f42-91be-8e286aaae05d",
          "conversation_id": "conversation_11aa81e3-f884-4bc2-9b0d-9c156d5a198e",
          "sender_principal_id": "human",
          "worker_id": null,
          "execution_id": null,
          "body": "After context replacement, inspect your retained research sources in this private conversation and use research_read to retrieve one original source. Give one supported fact, its original retrieval time and limitations. Do not search or open fresh web pages; do not share private history into a group.",
